#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:6
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:7
msgid ""
"This module, in conjunction with [interpret]-like objects can register "
"any file type the npm ecosystem has a module loader for. This library is "
"a dependency of [Liftoff]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:9
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:11
msgid "prepare(config, filepath, requireFrom)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:12
msgid ""
"Look for a module loader associated with the provided file and attempt "
"require it.  If necessary, run any setup required to inject it into "
"[require.extensions](http://nodejs.org/api/globals.html#globals_require_extensions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:14
msgid "`config` An [interpret]-like configuration object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:16
msgid "`filepath` A file whose type you'd like to register a module loader for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:18
msgid ""
"`requireFrom` An optional path to start searching for the module required"
" to load the requested file.  Defaults to the directory of `filepath`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:20
msgid ""
"If calling this method is successful (aka: it doesn't throw), you can now"
" require files of the type you requested natively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:22
msgid ""
"An error with a `failures` property will be thrown if the module "
"loader(s) configured for a given extension cannot be registered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:24
msgid "If a loader is already registered, this will simply return `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rechoir_README.md:26
msgid ""
"**Note:** While rechoir will automatically load and register transpilers "
"like `coffee-script`, you must provide a local installation. The "
"transpilers are **not** bundled with this module."
msgstr ""

